<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin says fall budget update due in Oct.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin says fall budget update due in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Monday he will reveal by how much he exceeded his 1995/96 deficit reduction targets when he presents his autumn budget update in October.</p>
<p>Martin told reporters after a session of parliament that he would give the exact number in the update.</p>
<p>He is widely expected to undershoot his fiscal 1995/96 (April-March) C$32.7 billion deficit target by at least C$2.5 billion of unused contingency reserve.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
</text>
